Build
=====

Packaging rules for 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS. Driver source is on main.

Install the build dependencies:

    sudo apt install build-essential debhelper dh-dkms device-tree-compiler

From debian/latest, with the local main branch up to date:

    builddir=$(mktemp -d)
    mkdir "$builddir/source"
    git archive main | tar -x -C "$builddir/source"
    cp -a debian "$builddir/source/"
    cd "$builddir/source"
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The .deb is generated in "$builddir". The upstream version in debian/changelog
must match PACKAGE_VERSION in main's dkms.conf.

Installation
============

Remove any previous source installation first. On the Raspberry Pi, run
this from the directory containing the built package. Replace PACKAGE.deb
with its actual filename.

    sudo apt install ./PACKAGE.deb

Configure the overlay in /boot/firmware/config.txt following main's README.

Uninstall:

    sudo apt purge rk628-rpi-dkms

Releasing
=========

Install the release tools and authenticate GitHub CLI:

    sudo apt install dpkg-dev devscripts gh
    gh auth login

Update PACKAGE_VERSION on main for a new driver release, commit and push.
Then, from debian/latest:

    ./release.sh --prepare

Edit the changelog entry, commit and push the packaging branch. Wait for
both source and packaging CI to pass, then:

    ./release.sh              # Preview the source and packaging tags
    ./release.sh --execute    # Create and push the tags
